{
  "id": "leader-tree",
  "title": "The leader tree",
  "description": "Every command grouped under one prefix key, so the whole registry costs one reservation instead of one per command. Included by every shipped preset, under Ctrl+Shift+Space, so choosing a preset never removes the route to a command that tool has no opinion about. The first chord is written `leader` and is substituted with whichever chord the preset declares. What is deliberately not here: the nine drawer segments, which would need a fourth chord and are one keystroke from their tab; the two mobile-only tab commands and the narrow-layout Settings drawer, which are gestures; and `session.open`, which is what clicking a row already does. All of them are in the palette and all of them are bindable.",
